# Backend env

Use the **repository root** `.env` (see `../.env.example`).

```sh
cp ../.env.example ../.env
make -C .. local-dev
# or:
make -C .. backend-dev
```

Production: `scripts/prod-env.sh init` writes `../.env.server` from
`../deploy/env/schema` (see `../docs/design/env-core.md`).

This file is intentionally empty of secrets.
